    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "STLA_1020",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Typical subway experience. Nothing great, nothing bad. Cheap sandwiches that are quick. The workers didn’t seem to be happy to be working but made the sandwiches as asked. If you need a quick lunch and not spend over $20 you can count on Subway.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Tabitha McLaughlin",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The restaurant is right across from our hotel.  The staff was friendly and the business was very clean.  We ate there several times during our vacation.  The food was very good.   I highly recommend this business and we will definitely be returning on our next vacation.",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Yes Hi",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "ABSOLUTELY AWFUL. i went and got bacon i did not want my bread toasted and the women gave me UNCOOKED BACON then said it wasn’t her fault because of me not saying to cook the bacon i shouldn’t have to ask. will not go back .",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Wolf Idk",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "They don’t PUT any OR just a little thing of mayonnaise LIKE WTH",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Stormi Brown",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "They are over charging! Went into this subway today, I ordered a 6 inch tuna sub and added drinks and chips. I noticed my total was more than it should have been. After I paid the cashier took my receipt and crumbled it up and pushed it over to the side which was weird, so I asked for it to see what exactly he charged me for. When I asked he didn’t give me a receipt and immediately goes back to his computer and calculator. He charged me PURPOSELY for double meat. He then goes to his tip jar (not",
        "time": "a year ago"
      }
