  {
    "place_id": "ChIJY7Zjm8wPmogRm1GlzllDIlI",
    "name": "Lambert's Cafe",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "2981 S McKenzie St, Foley, AL 36535, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-943-7655",
    "website": "http://www.throwedrolls.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5918366913316344219",
    "lat": 30.3707774,
    "lng": -87.68213829999999,
    "plus_code": "98C9+84 Foley, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.6,
    "reviews_count": 21084,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Gary Leemgraven",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Fun place to visit! A \"must\" to be sure. More food than you can eat! The Thrown Rolls are delicious. Fried Okra, black eyed peas, collard greens, macaroni and cheese with tomato sauce, apple butter and molasses. It more like a experience! Been in business since 1942 Hometown Favorite. Tourist spot, also has on site Souvenir store. Not far from Gulf Shores and Orange Beach.\nFun for the whole family.\nMeals were delicious as well. You will leave with a full belly! It was a adventure for sure. We wi",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "ViviAnn Lane",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "My new favorite place!!! The ambiance is really nice, the food is really good and the service was the Best! You get it all in this one place!! Our waitress, Monica was so nice and checked on us several times. The food arrived hot and pretty quick! Even all the pass arounds were served hot and tasty! I actually caught my roll!! I will definately be sharing my experience to all!!",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rafe Bar",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Really enjoyed everything we got, I recommend the ribeye, the fried chicken was good as well. Seems like a random item but is probably my favorite side is the pickled cucumbers and onions, very good! Cornbread was good as well, and can’t forget the throwed rolls! The rolls pair well with apple butter and sorghum. The only difference between here and the sikeston location is no gift shop.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Randall Deaton",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Lambert’s Cafe: A Southern Feast with a Flying Twist\nIf you’re heading to Lambert’s Cafe in Foley, Alabama, you need to come with a massive appetite and keep your head on a swivel. Famously known across the country as the \"Home of the Throwed Rolls,\" this lively and legendary institution is defined by its quirky, high-energy tradition of servers tossing warm, fluffy dinner rolls across the crowded dining room to eager guests. It is perhaps the only restaurant where playing with your food is not ",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rafael Mora",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Enjoyed my food. First time coming. They do throw those delicious bread rolls. The atmosphere is not as comfortable in my experience. This is a straight 4.5 in my book. Delicious southern food with a twist of fun. I would like to come back and try other plates. I would recommend the visit. The only thing is the understood, uncomfortable stare, from the locals and some staff. If there is a friendlier more welcoming to other ethnicities local I would give the absolute 5 stars.",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      }
    ],
