  {
    "place_id": "ChIJKaRD5v2nkIgRB_1fB_a3zR0",
    "name": "Pirates Cove",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "6664 Co Rd 95, Elberta, AL 36530, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-987-1224",
    "website": "http://www.piratescoveriffraff.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=2147574864639163655",
    "lat": 30.3217538,
    "lng": -87.5339626,
    "plus_code": "8FC8+PC Elberta, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 2647,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Shawn Shepherd",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Cool little local spot to grab food and drinks where you can pull up in your boat (dock or right onto the sand).\nThere's a small beach and an extra bar area with live music.\n\nI am not a local (yet 😉) and felt a little overdressed arriving with a collared polo, khaki shorts and tennis shoes. So feel free to come as you are with swim trunks and flip flops.\n\nThe food was good and the staff were friendly.\n\nThey probably need a little more help to keep things cleaned up and don't be surprised to see ",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brent Ryals",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great off the beaten path hangout. Mainly a boat up to place, we drove to it. The Bushwackers are great! So are the cheeseburgers. Can be busy at lunch. It's not classy, but a good atmosphere. Small beach for the kids to play on",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Phil R",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Second trip to Pirates Cove. Same as the first—still the same old waterfront dive bar that feels like it’s been frozen in time. If you’ve spent any time growing up around water with parents who just kind of let you roam free so they can drink in peace, you know exactly what I mean. Now that I’m an adult, I somehow find myself dragging my own kids to places like this, just so my wife and I can have a drink while the kids do their thing in what we’ll consider a “safe” environment.\n\nThe food… it’s ",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rick Koller",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "If you are into Dive bars this place is for you! We loved everything about this little place from the beach bar atmosphere to the open flame grilled burgers. Not to mention the tasty Drinks! We loved it so much we sent a group from our condo about 25-30 people to have a party! I did go there the week before to warn them lol! Thanks from our group to yours for being so gracious and inviting to us!!  Rick",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kerri Monroe-Stevens",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Haven’t eaten the food yet. Planning on it in near future, this is my newest treasure!! My pups ABSOLUTELY LOVE coming here, my little chihuahua loves to just roam and greet, while my other sweet blue heeler wants to play fetch! 🐾🥰💙",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
