  {
    "place_id": "ChIJQ5giJsgEmogRstxat76ZO1w",
    "name": "Original Oyster House Boardwalk",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "701 Gulf Shores Pkwy, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-2445",
    "website": "https://www.originaloysterhouse.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=6646074719514320050",
    "lat": 30.2545635,
    "lng": -87.68913859999999,
    "plus_code": "7836+R8 Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 7640,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Whitney Prince",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We have been here several times and it never fails to be a great experience. There is usually a wait, but they give you a buzzer and you can grab a drink and go do some shopping while you wait. I had raw oysters for an appetizer and the soft shell crab for my meal with baked potato and salad bar for sides. The others at the table got the shrimp bake, stuffed flounder and crab stuffed grouper. It was all cooked perfectly and delicious. Our server was Mr. Rogers, and he made our experience even mo",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Deepak Rao",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had the triple combination seafood dinner plate with shrimp scampi, blackened mahi mahi, and fried flounder. And the salad bar with a cup of gumbo.\n\nThe gumbo was packed with shrimp and sausage.\n\nAll of the seafood was par excellence!! The salad bar here is the simply the best in this area. The high turnover of customers ensures that they serve the finest and best food.\n\nThe service was very good. This is a long standing top notch restaurant and it continues to exceed our expectations every t",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Duke",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Good salad bar, fried mozzarella was good, liked that the marinara for them was served cold. The shell shocked oyster sampler was outstanding. My wife had the chicken Alfredo and it was good as well, it had too much sauce for her liking, but flavor was very good. Also had a side of cheese grits and they were outstanding.",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Craig Gaddy",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Food was good. Service was great. Salad bar was my favorite part. Gumbo was good.  It was a little cold. Beautiful setting though with good chance to talk. Everyone was so friendly.",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Teri-ann Blake",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Luncheon platter and Shrimp and Grits are Excellent. The sides Cole Slaw, Red Beans and Rice, the Greens are best ever. The Server was exceptional. We took home Bread pudding that was very Delicious.\n\nThe Scenery very beautiful and peaceful",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      }
    ],
    "price_level": 2,
