  {
    "place_id": "ChIJR1bZlp8HmogR2ro8KW2DA5M",
    "name": "Louisiana Lagniappe, Orange Beach, AL",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "27267 Perdido Beach Blvd #201, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-981-2258",
    "website": "http://www.thelouisianalagniappe.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10593455253372058330",
    "lat": 30.2767448,
    "lng": -87.5606483,
    "plus_code": "7CGQ+MP Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.6,
    "reviews_count": 966,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Terri Head",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had reservations for our Valentine’s Day dinner at 5:00. It was our first time to eat here. We were sat immediately and by the windows for a beautiful view of the bay. Our server was Eian. He and the other dining room workers were great. He was very knowledgeable about the dinner menu and our glasses were never empty.  We started with the lobster rangoon as an appetizer. My husband had the bayou grouper and I had the stuffed shrimp as entrees. All three dishes were excellent. I would recommen",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mary Mcd",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Great promotion....2 can dine for $59.  Two entrees plus bottle of wine.  I upgraded to steak for extra $10.  It was huge and perfectly cooked.  Spouse had jambalaya which was tasty but unfortunately had a few pieces of shrimp shell which detracted from the dish.  Service was excellent and atmosphere was lively.  Special promotion is only Sun to Thurs presently.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "jettt111",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This is my favorite place to eat at the beach. Everything is alway good. I love grouper and then add lump crab meat and lobster and it’s can’t be beat. I love the house made salad dressing and creamy deuce baked potato. My wife got the shrimp pasta. It was great and plenty of shrimp on it. I go 2 or 3 times per trip and get different things",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jesse Tischauser",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "So many great options on the menu at the Lagniappe.  We came for the Two Can Dine for $59 fall specials.  It’s a really great deal!  We ended up upgrading our bottle of wine for $10 more and got the Grouper Almondine for $8 additional and the Grouper Pecan for $8 additional.  So we ended up spending $85 plus taxes which was still a great deal for these two delicious meals with salads and a side.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Glenn Johnson",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great dining experience. We got the grouper dishes. I got the blackened and my wife got the pan seared. Both were great but I thought mine had more flavor. The hush puppies and twice baked potatoes hit the spot as well. The only issue here is a tight parking lot but it’s worth the visit here.",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      }
    ],
    "price_level": 3,
