  {
    "place_id": "ChIJs5Kz5JwHmogRyeMoXBx1gX8",
    "name": "Cobalt the Restaurant",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "28099 Perdido Beach Blvd, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-923-5300",
    "website": "http://www.cobaltrestaurant.net/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=9187753479478240201",
    "lat": 30.2779257,
    "lng": -87.54955170000001,
    "plus_code": "7FH2+55 Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 6722,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Amanda Major",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Cobalt is a restaurant, but originally it’s a color whose meaning is associated with calmness, often symbolizing luxury and tranquility. You’re surrounded by calming blues in Cobalt the restaurant at Alabama Point, right next to the Perdido Bay Bridge, just beautiful blue watery-hues everywhere to be seen. Sit outside when weather permits, and ask for a window table when it’s hot.🥗 We actually watched Cobalt being built while staying at Caribe one winter, we’ve been patrons that long, and it’s m",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mrs. Mac",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Spectacular views, especially at sunset sitting outside!\nThey offer a special menu from 4-7 with a great value for smaller portions between lunch/dinner).\n\nFood was good, service was beyond excellent. Plenty of seating from bar to booths to outside patio.\nDefinitely worth a stop here & enjoying a good meal.\n\nAlso have a nice sized gift shop with sweets & jewelry/shirts type items.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Thomas Hodges",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "STOP HERE NOW!!! This place is fabulous… everything from the food to the view. We had the shrimp and crab dip (only recommendation, I’d add lemon, so ask for a side of them), pecan crusted catfish, tuna melt and bread pudding. The pecan crusted catfish I was skeptical… but the crunch they get on it is wonderful (I only know one way to eat fried catfish and that’s with coleslaw, tartar sauce and hot sauce… it didn’t disappoint). It was just delicious, so do yourself a favor and give it a shot!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Irma Montarsi",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Was looking for a place that was different and something unique to the area. Was referred to this restaurant and can say it was amazing! Food, service and staff was outstanding! I had the BBQ Gulf Shrimp as an appetizer and Bronzed Grouper for the entree. Sooooooooo good!!!!! Had a virgin piña colada and for dessert I had the Creole Cheesecake. Just so good that it’ll fill you up! My server Kyle was awesome! Very friendly and attentive. The host Amber was very friendly and helpful along with Sav",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brendan James",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Tried Cobalt for the first time during a December trip to Orange Beach and it exceeded expectations. Even with a 45-minute wait, there was plenty of seating and a fun souvenir area to check out. I had the bronzed Gulf grouper and my wife ordered the fried shrimp—both were fantastic, and the grouper was one of the best meals I’ve ever had. Highly recommend and can’t wait to return on our next trip!",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      }
    ],
