  {
    "place_id": "ChIJQ3rGXrkEmogR0DxsYEWOW5Q",
    "name": "Island Pancake House",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "337 E Beach Blvd, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-2711",
    "website": "http://www.bwonthebeach.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10690294569115598032",
    "lat": 30.2484506,
    "lng": -87.6840205,
    "plus_code": "68X8+99 Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 2430,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "EJ W",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Really good location looking out at the beach while eating. It was a little busy, so it may take a while to get a seat or to be helped. The food was pretty standard decent breakfast fare. My eggs and sausage were good, but the pancakes were excellent and very thick! The staff was very friendly, just busy.",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Stacy Hampton",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This breakfast place was very good. The best pancakes I've had so far on this trip. It wasn't very busy so it was very quiet in there but we had a beautiful view of the gulf. Service was very good and it's definitely worth stopping here.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Gilbert B Mitchell",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had an amazing experience! Candy was absolutely delightful, providing exceptional service, and the food was simply delicious. We couldn’t resist trying the smoked alligator sausage from the menu, and it was a yummy treat! The beautiful view added to the atmosphere, and the entire staff was so friendly and welcoming. What a wonderful time!",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Drake Mathias",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Food was great and the view was beautiful. The lack of any sort of background music did make it awkwardly quiet. Our server while nice was very quiet and barely said more than 5 words the whole time. Overall a good breakfast restaurant if your allready nearby but nothing to go out of your way for",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Lisa Bowman",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Breakfast was delicious! My husband did the build your own pancakes with pecan filling and peach topping and my bite was outstanding! I had the Meat Lovers skillet and it was excellent! The biscuit I ordered was soft and fluffy with a crispy brown top, just the way I make it at home! Our server was attentive, thoughtful and very personable. Great breakfast spot right on the beach!",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      }
    ],
