  {
    "place_id": "ChIJ6VNVkr4EmogRaTPu5yA61fM",
    "name": "Sea N Suds",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "405 E Beach Blvd, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-7894",
    "website": "http://www.sea-n-suds.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=17570013434260370281",
    "lat": 30.24814319999999,
    "lng": -87.68088519999999,
    "plus_code": "68X9+7J Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.3,
    "reviews_count": 3848,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Dee C",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "It's very casual.  Crab claws on the menu!! Pricey but good. Mullet all you can eat Tues and Friday not on the menu.  Great mullet.  Good hushpuppies and coleslaw.\nI'll be back",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Sarah Buchanan",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Sea N Suds is one of my absolute favorite restaurants in Gulf Shores! My family and I have been coming here for over 25 years. The food and service has been consistently good for as long as I can remember. Whether you are just coming off the beach for a quick lunch or heading out for a family dinner, Sea N Suds has something for you.\nI always enjoy my meal with a cup of their plentiful seafood gumbo and a glass of sweet iced tea. Leading up to our most recent trip to Gulf Shores, I was literally",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rae J",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "I think the seafood itself was just okay. The gumbo was delicious. The crab claws were my favorite item I tried. I think the ambiance of the restaurant is what makes this restaurant better than it is. Our server was really nice and helpful but disappeared towards the end of our stay. We needed a box and he never showed up again. A different server gave us a box.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "owen Utsey",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Sea-N-Suds in Gulf Shores is a casual, waterfront seafood restaurant that delivers fresh, flavorful dishes in a relaxed, friendly atmosphere. Known for its Gulf Coast favorites, the menu features fresh shrimp, oysters, fish sandwiches, and platters, all prepared with care and generous portions. Daily specials and seasonal offerings keep the menu interesting for repeat visitors, while sides like hush puppies, fries, and coleslaw complement the seafood perfectly.\n\nThe setting is informal and welco",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Michele Coffey",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Visited multiple times, mullet special ,fish dinner and seafood platter. Really good seafood, cod was great. Nice that you could get a non alcoholic frozen drink!!! Would hit this place daily♥️ sunset was incredible!!",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      }
    ],
