  {
    "place_id": "ChIJGQpKqbAEmogRw2CWr5jWnAY",
    "name": "Pink Pony Pub",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "137 E Gulf Pl, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-6371",
    "website": "http://www.pinkponypub.net/?utm_source=gbp&utm_medium=organic",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=476491611863670979",
    "lat": 30.2477973,
    "lng": -87.6875522,
    "plus_code": "68X6+4X Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.1,
    "reviews_count": 4305,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "LandyLane Boutique",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We’re visiting from Kentucky and stopped into Pink Pony Pub tonight on a busy Friday night, and I want to make sure management sees this.\n\nWe were told three staff members had called off, and this young lady had already been working since around 10 AM and was still going strong when we were there around 8 PM. She stayed to help so customers wouldn’t suffer.\n\nShe definitely went above and beyond. She was incredibly kind, friendly, attentive, and never once let the stress of the night show. Her at",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "ARTS",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "I'll start by saying the food and drinks were good. Our server was good, but not friendly. I love crab cakes, so naturally thats what I ordered. $21 on the menu- no problem. Then she says it DOESNT COME WITH A SIDE!!😳 That was an expensive crab!! We chose to eat here because we were staying at the hotel there, but I dont believe we would choose here again if not for that. The red lights on the patio gave off the strangest hue and made all our food look funny.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kylie Droke",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "John was our server and was amazing! Not too much, not too little. I had the cheeseburger on sourdough and it was definitely a hit. My sister got the nachos(great shareable plate) and tasted wonderful. A must in Gulf Shores!!!",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rachel Buell",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We stopped here while spending time at the Gulf Shores beach. Cute pink building close by to the beach, with a nice view. The staff was friendly and the food came out pretty quickly. My group and I all really liked our food. They got fried gulf shrimp and blackened gulf shrimp. The hush puppies were delicious. The best any of us have had anytime recently. The fries were seasoned and perfectly crispy. I ordered the blackened fish basket and it was as delicious as I could’ve hoped for.",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Gary Leemgraven",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Fun Beach Bar, actually on the Beach! Food was delicious. They do have outdoor seating, but it was filled when we went. Parking is Pay in the lots next door. You can park for free across the street. Busy place so you may have a wait.\nBut worth it",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      }
    ],
    "price_level": 2,
