  {
    "place_id": "ChIJaym-x7YEmogR0U8amdLTFS8",
    "name": "De Soto's Seafood Kitchen",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "138 W 1st Ave, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-7294",
    "website": "https://www.desotosseafoodkitchen.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=3392850795758768081",
    "lat": 30.24954769999999,
    "lng": -87.6914411,
    "plus_code": "68X5+RC Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 5501,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Jimmy Krueger",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We enjoyed a nice lunch here recently. The place has a lot of seating inside. We sat downstairs and had plenty of room to spread out in our booth with our group of 6. The complimentary bread was tasty. The smoked tuna dip was a great starter. It had really good flavor and the crostini bread that came with it was great. My daughter enjoyed her fried shrimp and applesauce off the kids menu. My wife loved her blackened catfish. We were there when happy hour was going on (11-6) so we tried a couple ",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Deepak Rao",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Excellent all around. Very reasonably priced winter specials till March 1.\n\nWe had the blackened grouper with baked potato and fried green tomatoes. And the blackened trigger with sweet potato casserole and steamed vegetables.\n\nEverything was delicious and the service was absolutely the best possible!!\n\nDeSoto has been a favorite for many years and continues to exceed our expectations!!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Vikas Chilkuri",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had a great experience here! Kasey was our server and she handled it like a champ. We had 2 kids meals 2 appetizers and an big platter to share, our tab was $90 something with tip.\nThe food was great, not the regular commercial  beach/pier food you see nowadays in touristy areas. We loved it and will come back when we come back to the area. 😍😍💯",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Moore Explores",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Without question the best seafood (maybe best restaurant) in Gulf Shores. The Grouper (blackened) was phenomenal, the popcorn shrimp perfection, but the sides (I went with fried green tomato’s, slaw, and turnip greens) made the meal.\n\nService was great - atmosphere fun and friendly - clean and family oriented.\n\nCouldn’t recommend the place enough - was in town for 3 days and ate meals here twice.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Shannon Schenk",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Busy, but delicious.  Waitress had several large parties and wait time while seated was long.  The bread was delicious!  I also had alligator bites and coconut shrimp, both were wonderful as were their sauces.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      }
    ],
    "price_level": 2,
