    "plus_code": "7CR8+67 Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 1640,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Teresa Peters",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Big Fish is our favorite restaurant in the Orange Beach area. They have so different kinds of fish & options on how to prepare it. The presentation is always beautiful! We ate here only once last year while visiting and when going this year, Chris remembered us and said: Hey, you are my Iowa friends. That tells you how good the service is. We are eating there tonight for our 3rd time this visit! Picture is the bronzed grouper. I did substitute the spinach for green beans. Ask for the Cilantro li",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Implant-R-Us",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The Sashimi Sampler & Rainbow roll was phenomenal. The fish was so tender you savored every bite. We also had the firecracker shrimp fired rice was tasty.  I couldn't have asked for a better way to end my night.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jason Zeleny",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Big Fish is probably our favorite restaurant to go to when we're down at Orange Beach, AL. No matter what you order on the menu, it's always amazing. Even my daughter's grilled cheese was awesome (and I don't usually like grilled cheese). I do recommend a reservation as this spot is popular.\n\nWe ordered a couple of the fresh catches of the day finished with the Big Fish style topping, fire cracker shrimp (with added spice), ribeye steak, and grilled cheese. Thanks for the amazing and memorable d",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Emily",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The food is absolutely divine! I highly recommend the grouper with the asian twist. The cucumbers were also outstanding, and the sushi was a hit. We love coming here and can't wait to come back!",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Nikki Wilson",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "6 top there for a birthday party and we had: appetizers of beef tataki, seaweed salad, cucumber salad, dumplings, and crab claws. The only seasoning on anything of those dishes was the sesame oil on the beef. Then we each got entrees and drinks. I can’t speak to what everyone thought about their entrees, but…\nI worked for a sushi restaurant in college, so I can tell just by looking at a spicy tuna roll whether or not it will be good. And when they sat my plate down I was bummed.\nOverall, not a b",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
