  {
    "place_id": "ChIJ6f0Gm7kEmogR3oTbx_7JVQM",
    "name": "Hooters",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "300 E Beach Blvd, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-4668",
    "website": "https://www.hooters.com/locations/31005-gulf-shores?utm_source=google&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=gmb-website-cta-gulf+shores-al-gulf+shores",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=240320251246118110",
    "lat": 30.2491614,
    "lng": -87.68564459999999,
    "plus_code": "68X7+MP Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 3.5,
    "reviews_count": 1670,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "G B",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Quite, cozy and friendly. The food  was fresh hot and delicious. There was no line and no waiting and our waitress deserved every penny of her tip. Also kudos to the cook who had our food well sauced, seasoned and temperature hot. GHOST PEPPER for me and Lemon Pepper for the lady. BTW make sure if you are a Veteran let them know before you let them bring you the ticked they offer 15% and not the average 10%.\n\nThanks guys and continue the good work. BRAVO ZULU!!!!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Bean NeFF",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This was our first time here and it was an amazing experience!! The food was great, definitely one of the best Hooters I’ve been to. Our waitress, Jerzie, was outstanding! She was very friendly and a great server. Definitely recommend this place if you’re stopping by in Gulf Shores, Alabama.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "JGordonSUX",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The Best Little Hooters In Alabama.\n\nI've visited Hooters establishments literally around the world since before 2006. I don't know how many stores over the years. I've been to The World's First, World's Biggest, but today, I visited The World's Tiniest.\n\nTo me, this is where the charm is. I visited during lunch and dinner. Both times I was greeted wonderfully by the servers. There are only 11 tables inside, and 6 outside.\n\nIt shows that the kitchen staff cares about their product. Food was hot ",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kelly Knight",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "I’m a boy mom of 4 from Louisiana and Hooters is our our go-to place to eat on a weekly basis, so when we came to GS for vacation, our dinner decision was a no brainer. The service was ok. But the food was Horrible!  We ordered our usual order of fries with a side of queso along with buffalo chicken dip as our appetizer. when we got it, the fries were old/stale and cold. So we sent them back and the cook took the same old-stale fries and put them back in the grease, heated, and reserved them to ",
        "time": "10 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Michelle F.",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "First night on vacation with my daughter and after a full day she wants Hooters for dinner, so we ordered in.  She ordered the buffalo chicken dip....for $18 and change!!  I knew it was all going sideways when  they neglected to even send her order with the rest of the food!!!  Can someone please make this make sense, see pictures!!!  How in the heck are the two tiny cups in the pictures worth over $18???  MAKE THIS MAKE SENSE!!!  Never again!  DO BETTER HOOTERS!!!!!!!!!!!!!",
        "time": "a year ago"
      }
    ],
