  {
    "place_id": "ChIJY8DmnW2vkIgRmak-3jk3sjY",
    "name": "Perdido Key Sports Bar & Restaurant",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "13583 Perdido Key Dr, Pensacola, FL 32507, USA",
    "phone": "+1 850-332-6403",
    "website": "http://perdidokeysportsbar.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=3941273345583917465",
    "lat": 30.30197179999999,
    "lng": -87.42689949999999,
    "plus_code": "8H2F+Q6 Pensacola, FL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 1283,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Jordan Love",
        "rating": 2,
        "text": "We were pretty disappointed. It took 20 minutes just to have our order taken, we were never checked on, and we never even received a ticket. My grilled chicken made me sick afterward, and my friend’s chili dog came out cold with unmelted shredded cheese.\n\nThe place was extremely dark inside and felt very out of place compared to the beach area. The ranch and Coke were the only positives.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "William Wright",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Came here for a quick snack and got the Blackened Mahi Salad for only $14! So many other things I wanted to try. Great variety of bar snacks, sandwiches and wings/burgers. Cold beer, always happy daily from 12-6 with awesome bartenders! Also located right near the beach. Great to come and have a casual relaxed dinning experience without breaking the bank! True sports bar lots of tvs!",
        "time": "10 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Monica Stephanie",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "If you are looking for a \"Cheers\" episode type of vibe, this is it. Everyone was friendly. The draft beer was cold. I had the mushrooms and they were even good. Their prices are also good. Full bar and menu. A lot of TVs around to watch any sport you can think of. The servers/bartenders are very attentive and have great personalities. You'll really enjoy this place. Can't wait for football season! I will be back",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Chris Brooks",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Can’t speak on the whole menu as I only had the fried chicken balls (pretty good), but everything here is cheap. I had an appetizer, a draft beer and 2 cocktails for under $25. It’s a fun little dive bar worth stopping at if you’re in the area.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "leticia skae",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "1) Marissa (our server) was amazing! She was super nice and attentive 5⭐️\n2) Flavorful food (highly recommend their chicken jalapeño fried balls) 5⭐️\n3) Prices and portion sizes 5⭐️ especially since this place is really close to the beach and not as over priced as other spots\n4) The rude server behind the bar wearing a red shirt, with a dark haired ponytail, who is only kind to locals—as she talks to them and ignores you when you try to tell her your family is seated outside—will huff at you and",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      }
    ],
