  {
    "place_id": "ChIJm1Se2l6vkIgRO_z21TELAZY",
    "name": "The Point Restaurant",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "14340 Innerarity Point Rd, Pensacola, FL 32507, USA",
    "phone": "+1 850-492-3577",
    "website": "http://thepointperdido.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10808932889336937531",
    "lat": 30.3152861,
    "lng": -87.4450011,
    "plus_code": "8H83+4X Pensacola, FL, USA",
    "rating": 4.6,
    "reviews_count": 1503,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Fernando Damus",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "I absolutely love this place for different reasons. This time, we took our own fish and they cooked for us, and it was AMAZING. Service is always fantastic, food is superb and the whole atmosphere is great and super relaxed. They usually have some bands playing there and it is so enjoyable. You will have a great experience, guaranteed!",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Stephanie Thompson",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Had dinner on a Thursday evening when they a had a band playing wonderful music! Enjoyed the combination appetizer platter- fried green tomatoes, alligator bites and fried crab claws. Our entrees were delicious as well- the Royal red shrimp dinner and the special which was Royal red shrimp in  a Cajun brown butter sauce. Our server Shaylah was awesome. A must try. Great food and atmosphere.",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Christine Lipscomb",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "You've heard it said that beauty is only skin deep. While lacking somewhat in curb appeal and upscale decor, the meals we enjoyed there were equal to Cobalt or any other restaurant we've tried in Orange Beach or Gulf Shores. We got started with bar drinks and 2 appetizers. My entree was a platter featuring fried oysters, grilled grouper, scallops, hush puppies, baked potato and vegetable of the day (green beans). The homemade tartar sauce is very good. My husband had the fresh fish and 2 sides. ",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Cassandra Evans",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "We had the gumbo, coconut, shrimp, and the red fish special with grilled shrimp and mushroom gravy on top. The onion rings were good. Everything we had was delicious . We had excellent service from our server Ryan.",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Nancy Smith",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "I rarely leave negative reviews, but this experience at The Pointe in Gulf Breeze, Florida was absolutely unacceptable. The hostess, Jazzy, was extremely rude, dismissive, and unprofessional from the moment we arrived.\n\nWe were there to celebrate my sister’s birthday, which should have been a happy and memorable occasion. Instead, Jazzy’s attitude and behavior completely ruined her day. She spoke to us with obvious irritation, made us feel unwelcome, and acted as if we were a burden for simply b",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      }
    ],
