  {
    "place_id": "ChIJa8xq0_YGmogRLQ3xgRtOggQ",
    "name": "China Dragon",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "25405 Perdido Beach Blvd #19, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-269-0359",
    "website": "http://www.chinadragonorangebeach.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=324908003175238957",
    "lat": 30.2693813,
    "lng": -87.5912919,
    "plus_code": "7C95+QF Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4,
    "reviews_count": 480,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "TALIA Will Tell Ya",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Being semi-new year-round residents of Gulf Shores, we were so looking forward to finding good Chinese. I realize it's the low season (I have Iived at other beaches year round). My husband stated that his was decent, typical run of the mill. I thought it would be more than mediocre take-out Chinese. Especially, since it is a FSR (full-service restaurant). Very clean. Service was great. However, we won't be back. Other customers left reviews that they highly enjoyed, which is great. Unfortunately",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Bethany Lawrence",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Walking distance from our Hotel. The food is So Good! I had walnut chicken and my husband Mongolian beef. We both ate off each others plates. The server was a sweet heart.",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Maksim Blair",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Overall okay experience, I went due to them being open on Sunday. The food left much to be desired, especially for the price! The service wasn’t all the friendliest. No music also made it awkward feeling on the inside.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Ting Zhu",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "My husband and I visited our mom and dad in Orange Beach and decided to have lunch at a local Chinese restaurant called China Dragon. What a fantastic choice! We ordered four appetizers, three entrees, and a dessert, and every single dish was absolutely amazing. Owners are super friendly as well!\n\nThe first thing that caught our attention was the beautiful decor. The restaurant’s classic Chinese architectural design, paired with the thoughtful display of traditional instruments on the walls, cre",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Barry Reed",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We ordered four different entrees and all three soups. Everything was delicious. The egg rolls have the thinnest crispiest crust, perfection!",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      }
    ],
    "price_level": 1,
