  {
    "place_id": "ChIJJxlDQV6vkIgRskWUk74U9L8",
    "name": "Hub Stacey's at The Point",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "5851 Galvez Rd, Pensacola, FL 32507, USA",
    "phone": "+1 850-497-0071",
    "website": "https://www.hubstaceyspensacolaperdido.com/menu",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=13831703164313945522",
    "lat": 30.31457199999999,
    "lng": -87.4419479,
    "plus_code": "8H75+R6 Pensacola, FL, USA",
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 2334,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Featherbear19",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Absolutely loved this place! We came here to grab lunch while vacationing in Perdido Key and we are so glad we did! Delaney, our server, was excellent! She was so friendly, attentive, and quite funny too. The food was delicious and we will definitely go back when we are in the area. The view is beautiful as well!!!",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "k beard",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Fun waterside bar/restaurant. NOTE: Bikers-parking is gravel/dirt. Also- do NOT bring your pets. They will ask you to leave.\nStaff was friendly, food was delicious and atmosphere is fantastic!",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Meagan Kosbab",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Wow this is a must! We got the sampler app first which did not disappoint. For dinner we ordered the cheeseburger that got 2 thumbs up along with the boss baby. We also split their giant BLT and holy wow it was huge. Their potato salad is good but just know it's more of a loaded flavor. Bonus that the pieces are extremely reasonable.\nWe will definitely be back.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Fernando Damus",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "I actually really like this place. Every time we are at Perdido we try to go. It is a very unique place where service, atmosphere and food work very well. I always order any of the sandwiches but I also hear that the wings are great. Sometimes there’s a band playing music. They have a bar and tv’s so you get the whole package. I totally recommend it!",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Serena Caldeyro",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "It was okay. Nice atmosphere nicer if sitting outside. All the food looked good. They don't serve seafood only tuna salad. We were working from out of town & my son found this place. I  had my heart set on steamed  old bay shrimp but they don't serve seafood. Definitely bar food. Prices for beer decent, food for what some in our party ordered didn't meet expectations vs price. Muffala, mushroom burger, sampler, onion rings, wings & kids tenders all average, no complaints.",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      }
    ],
