    "place_id": "ChIJefev2IUamogRggeR4Pxoy5w",
    "name": "The Tin Top Restaurant & Oyster Bar",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "17451 County Rd 49 S, Bon Secour, AL 36511, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-949-5086",
    "website": "http://www.tintoprestaurant.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=11298239525497669506",
    "lat": 30.311489,
    "lng": -87.7259924,
    "plus_code": "876F+HJ Bon Secour, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 4164,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Rick Etterling",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "TinTop was superb.   The food was excellent and the facility was in excellent condition.   Our service was outstanding. Meagan S. was our server.   She provided top quality service, excellent knowledge of the menu and made suggestions that we top notch.   My wife got the crab cakes which she loved and finished it off with strawberry bread pudding.   I had the all you can eat shrimp and fried mullet.   Delicious. We will definitely be back next time in town.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Roni Burgett",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "The food was good. I was not as impressed as I thought. The fish tacos were just plain. I was hoping for more flavor. I do want to try other dishes to see if lack of flavor is all the time or just that day. Not crazy about the portions either. There is a store onsite to purchase many things. The waterfront makes it a beautiful place to watch the sunset. This place is very isolated. We did however have an amazing waiter. He went above and beyond and the manager stopped by to make sure everyone wa",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jimmy Krueger",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We tried this place recently for lunch and it was good. There was a lot of seating on the outdoor patio and several tables inside. They have a wide variety of options. The smoked tuna dip was a great starter. The red fish and grilled shrimp po boy were excellent. There was so much shrimp on the po boy I couldn't eat it as a sandwich, which I thought was great. Service was excellent. The new location is awesome right on the water.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Zoe Gehman",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Amazing dinner at Tin Top! The fresh catch of the day was tripletail fish and I had the pecan encrusted fresh catch with collard greens and Gouda cheese grits. My girlfriends had the blackened fresh catch, and seared fresh catch with fried okra and Lima beans. Everything was so good. The view is so good and the seats out on the deck are a great vibe.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "SKH",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had a phenomenal experience at Tin Top. The food was delicious and the atmosphere is great. Perfect for an intimate dinner or big event, Tin Top is an excellent place for dinner. We had Ashton as our server. She was so attentive, conversational, and anticipated our needs. Wonderful service. The crab claws are pricey but you get a ton and are probably the best in Baldwin county. I had the pecan crusted trigger fish in crawfish sauce. Do yourself a favor and get this. The kids menu has excellen",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      }
    ],
