  {
    "place_id": "ChIJK4TikwoHmogRxGwlt2_gRZI",
    "name": "Latitude 30",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "27200 Perdido Beach Blvd, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-981-9811",
    "website": "http://www.perdidobeachresort.com/dining/latitude-30",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=10540077273349188804",
    "lat": 30.2732153,
    "lng": -87.5615907,
    "plus_code": "7CFQ+79 Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.1,
    "reviews_count": 226,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Kay",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Such a great restaurant inside of this wonderful resort! We ate here several times on our stay during the summer. The service was fast, the staff were friendly and the food was always fresh and so delicious with filling portion sizes! My husband tried his 1st ever chicken n waffles here!",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Marshae Black",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Located inside Perdido Beach Resort. We had a really good time dining here. Very kid friendly menu. We ordered appetizers (Spin Dip and Steak Fries), kids Shrimp Alfredo, shrimp and grits, fish tacos (served with sweet potato tots) and a bacon burger. All of the food was tasty. The service was a little slow, but she was very friendly. Prices weren’t too bad either. Even with bar drinks a party of 4 ate for $150.",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jeremiah DuPree",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Okay, food. It's not bad, it's not fantastic either. It's better than any fast food, guaranteed, and it's slightly above par for a sit-down restaurant.\n\nI would say the breakfast is better than the lunch or dinner entrees.\n\nThe staff is fantastic, friendly and accommodating. The environment/atmosphere is pleasant also. It is a part of Perdido Beach Resort.\n\nYou can dine in if you are not staying at the resort as a patron. However, there is no overnight parking available for non patrons of the re",
        "time": "2 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Dan Reamer",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We were pleasantly surprised with this restaurant.  The menu was a bit small but had many good options.  For a resort restaurant, the prices were really reasonable, and the food was really good.  The staple though is Miss Glinda’s omelet bar.  Only available on the weekends from what I understand but well worth the stop!",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Amanda Riendeau",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Spacious restaurant inside Perdido Beach Resort. Food was fresh, Grouper tacos were excellent! Quick, friendly service. Since I'm staying here for a few days I will most likely be back there before I leave.\nAsk for Melvin. Personable, kind & helpful waiter! He made the experience for sure!",
        "time": "3 years ago"
      }
    ],
