  {
    "place_id": "ChIJB8tsOpsGmogRg1lcanY1cz8",
    "name": "Ruby Slipper",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "24151 Perdido Beach Blvd, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-360-2400",
    "website": "https://www.rubybrunch.com/?olonwp=JjBtp_vMLk25gkYh_bnoiQ",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=4572056829418035587",
    "lat": 30.2634521,
    "lng": -87.6123511,
    "plus_code": "797Q+93 Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 4623,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Marlena",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Local here. Food is mediocre at best. Bacon and gravy were pretty good. Chicken was tasty. Biscuits were dry and hard on the bottom. Beignets were hard, burnt, and extremely dry. Espresso machine was down, so no good hot drink with our food. Waitress was inattentive. Overall we were extremely disappointed.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Amanda Major",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The Ruby Slipper Cafe on Perdido Beach Blvd in Orange Beach, Alabama, is open from breakfast through lunch. The chain originated in New Orleans, and they say they add some New Orleans flair to all their dishes. Some of their most popular orders include Blackstone and Cochon Eggs, BBQ Shrimp & Grits, and Bananas Foster French Toast. For those wanting something more potent to go with your meal, they have  Bloody Marys or Mimosas. The decor is cute, with space for dining inside and out, and the bat",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Scott Andrews",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Exceptional breakfast location right in Gulf Shores, Alabama.\nOur server was fast, friendly and cheerful.\nThe omelette was perfectly prepared and filled, and the cat’s  had biscuit was a perfect addition to the plate. I ate every bit of it!\nThe atmosphere is loud enough if you bring your children, but not enough if you wanna have a quiet cup of coffee for breakfast\nRecommended",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Charlene Ray",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Crystal was a wonderful server and very nice and knowledgeable of the menu. She gave us some great suggestions of menu favorites. It was a great dining experience and I would highly recommend The Ruby Slipper!!!",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "William Wright",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Came here today to surprise my Dad with a little treat. Was immediately greeted by Nate the bartender. Had my pup with me so we chose to sit in the patio lounge area. Crystal, was very friendly and recommended we get the Eggs Cochon Chicken St Charles. AMAZING!! Been here a couple times this WEEK. Service is always A-1. Please try the biscuits n gravy if you’re in town. Also, full bar service and a HUGE dinning area. Guess I’ll be back tomorrow😎",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      }
    ],
