  {
    "place_id": "ChIJl3-4HvoGmogRxW780ieqm60",
    "name": "Moe's Original BBQ",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "25603 Perdido Beach Blvd, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-981-7427",
    "website": "https://www.moesoriginalbbq.com/lo/orange-beach/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=12509779477971889861",
    "lat": 30.2693676,
    "lng": -87.5904243,
    "plus_code": "7C95+PR Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.6,
    "reviews_count": 1949,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "A. B.",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We found this awesome BBQ by smell. Sounds weird, but we could smell it long before we knew what it was and the smell sold us instantly.\n\nWe made the 1/2 mile trek down Perdido Beach Blvd and found it, the holy grail hidden amongst unsuspecting chain restaurants. From the stickers on the door to the awesome signs out front - we knew we were in for something good.\n\nThe nachos: amazing\n\nThe pulled pork: the most tender, fall apart pulled pork we have ever had. Anywhere (from Kansas City and beyond",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "BETH Dawson",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "My family and I loved Moe's! I love the laid-back atmosphere. There's seating available inside and outside. There's lots of cool art and pictures on the wall that I enjoyed looking at. The staff was friendly and helpful when ordering.\nI had the loaded baked potato with smoked chicken, and it was delicious and very filling.\nI tried the Ribs my husband ordered (I forgot to get a pic), but they were tender and flavorful.\nThe children enjoyed chicken tenders, grilled cheese, fried Catfish, mac & che",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "William McIntyre",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Normally I shy away from a chain BBQ place. But, the past reviews were correct. The pork had a nice smokey flavor. The service was outstanding. The chocolate Orea pudding was a nice side. It looked like many locals were they, which is a good sign. The atmosphere was very creative.",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "DL",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Great food and a fun atmosphere to dine in. Unfortunately, they often run out of certain menu choices almost every time we are there. We keep going back though.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mark",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Had a very good lunch here. The wife got the pulled pork sandwich which was very good and I got the sausage sandwich and fries. It was really tasty. They use Conecuh Sausage which if you haven’t had it you need to get some!! The outside has a nice atmosphere.",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      }
    ],
