  {
    "place_id": "ChIJtWvLtCAFmogRenDIewwqX_0",
    "name": "Big Beach Brewing",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "300 E 24th Ave, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-2337",
    "website": "http://bigbeachbrewing.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=18257357647487987834",
    "lat": 30.2782115,
    "lng": -87.6828105,
    "plus_code": "78H8+7V Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.8,
    "reviews_count": 764,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Snow Gypsies Travelers",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had Fun here!! we sat by the Fireplace listen to some Great music 🎵 Buy Billy Bones!! awesome Beer 🍻 and Wine 🍷 great time great place great location.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "William Atkins",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great brewery with wonderful bartenders! The beers were excellent! I didn't try the sours so I can't speak to those but all the others were good or great! Plus boiled peanuts! I'd never had them before so this was a new and very welcome experience. I had to post a picture of the taps because they are individually crafted glass. I would have posted a photo of the wonderful bartenders but I didn't ask their permission to post their images.",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Carla Morrin",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "The beers were great, however the blond woman serving us at the bar was super rude both times we went to the counter She wouldn't answer questions and acted like we were inconveniencing her. The food was good too. Very disappointing! There is no reason to treat us like that when we got beers, food, and merchandise.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Michael Cornelison",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "As a person that has visited many breweries, Big Beach Brewing hit all marks. Fun atmosphere, quick and friendly staff and great beer. They have a wide selection of easy drinking beers to fun and creative beers with full flavor. I left with a six pack to take home. I would highly recommend if you are in the Gulf Shores area to stop in and check out some of their artisanal craft beers.",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Paul Fenrich",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This is a must stop if you are into craft beers. We tried four different beers, and they were all delicious.  The bartender was very nice, and he had a lot of knowledge of their products. The atmosphere was great. We sat outside on the upper deck and then moved downstairs. The weather was perfect, and the boys found a new friend to play cars with. Very kid friendly, several families were hanging out.",
        "time": "2 years ago"
      }
    ],
