  {
    "place_id": "ChIJrfq8Vv8OmogRoOfR6HZPcBc",
    "name": "Groovy Goat",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "106 S Owa Blvd A, Foley, AL 36535, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-999-4628",
    "website": "http://owa.groovygoat.us/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=1688937232394741664",
    "lat": 30.3741586,
    "lng": -87.6577191,
    "plus_code": "98FR+MW Foley, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4,
    "reviews_count": 1924,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Karen Sepko",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Came to Groovy Goat for an event!  Event room is through the Arcade to the left.  I never knew it was there!  Great space for 70 people 7 tables of 10 people.  Food was buffet style included sprimp/chicken/mixed vegetables/ fettuccine Alfredo/ mixed salad and… the best ever chocolate chip cookies!!",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Colleen Daugherty",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Lots of beers on tap and a large arcade for kiddos. Great for large parties both family and adult. Lots of TVs and “the game” you want to see is always on. As far as quality of the food….is hit or miss for both lunch and dinner service: scores average overall with positives being portion size and southern-inspired side options, like black eyed peas, while negatives include sloppy food presentation paired with what I will describe as inconsistent kitchen technique. Order the right thing and it’s ",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Wade Bombenger",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Damn. Thanks for the suggestion, Wade. The Redfish Sandwich struck a nerve. I grew up on Redfish in Florida. My mom would put potatoes in the oven and challenge me to catch dinner. Then I caught Red Snapper. We ate when the potatoes were done.\nThank you.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Nicole Brown",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Food was very over priced for the quality and amount received. We ordered a cob salad (which didn’t even come out with the corn) and the chicken tender plate. The chicken tenders were $17. They were very small and chewy (over cooked) and the fries were bright yellow and appeared to be old and stale. I usually don’t write or leave a bad review but I don’t recommend this restaurant. Service was fantastic, but food did not reflect this.",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Deborah R Harton",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "We attended a team party in a reserved room after the state cup soccer tournament this past weekend.  There were at least 70 guests and they had 1 waitress to take all orders/drinks.  An hour and a half after taking orders and bringing out everyone's food she brings out 2 children's hamburger plates (we ordered the adult burgers) and those burgers and 5 fries (literally) made an Aldi frozen hamburger patty look like filet mignon.  We still did not have our appetizer Nachos to share,  which we ha",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      }
    ],
