  {
    "place_id": "ChIJBVMOJfiokIgRX9XIu-SwCTQ",
    "name": "Crab Trap Perdido Key",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "16495 Perdido Key Dr, Pensacola, FL 32507, USA",
    "phone": "+1 850-492-8888",
    "website": "https://www.crabtrapflorida.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=3749722661212181855",
    "lat": 30.2851999,
    "lng": -87.49819079999999,
    "plus_code": "7GP2+3P Pensacola, FL, USA",
    "rating": 3.9,
    "reviews_count": 2791,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Gary Leemgraven",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Good menu, prices are a bit on the higher side. Server was very pleasant and attentive. Great location right off the beach.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Craig Kuehl",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Very nice first visit here. Food was all excellent.  Service was outstanding by our server Cassie. We had the Alaskan King Crab Legs x 2 orders which were awesome. Wife ordered the Bairdi Crab which was recommended and it was actually better than the King Crab, both were amazing though. Would highly recommend trying this location despite the negative reviews we read. Everything was great!!",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Drew Crouse",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great hot crab dip is incredible with the fried pita bread. Crabcake were exceptional.  And the Cajun chicken pasta is still my favorite",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Cheryl",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "My family was looking for a restaurant with food we all could eat since some are pickier than others. The Crab Trap satisfied that requirement. We went there around noon and found parking right away. The parking seemed adequate but it might fill up with those not going to the restaurant.\n\nWe were given a choice of indoor or outdoor dining since the restaurant wasn't full. Our host gave my child a bucket to keep that included a shovel, wicki sticks with the menu.\n\nWhile we waited for our food, we",
        "time": "10 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Dawn Badeaux",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "As a local seafood enthusiast who’s somehow managed to avoid The Crab Trap until now, I had high hopes based on glowing recommendations from friends. Spoiler alert: it was an experience.\n\nFrom the moment we walked in, the hostess and a young sidekick seemed more captivated by the latest episode on their phones than by actual guests — a distraction that lasted our entire visit. Maybe they were live-tweeting our arrival? Who knows.\n\nOur server, thankfully, made a swift appearance and took our drin",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      }
    ],
