  {
    "place_id": "ChIJZQQ0OicFmogRY_Wk7X98pQ0",
    "name": "Tacky Jacks Gulf Shores",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "240 E 24th Ave, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-8881",
    "website": "http://tackyjacks.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=983328982540023139",
    "lat": 30.2787094,
    "lng": -87.6836932,
    "plus_code": "78H8+FG Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 7218,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "jeff robichaud",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Tacky says it all but in a cool way. Food was excellent and atmosphere was fun and lively. Excellent outside play area for kids also. Our server/bartender was Michael (Navy Vet) and he had an outstanding personality and was a fantastic employee. Definitely deserved the 25% tip. We will definitely come again.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Karen Cordova",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Good breakfast, even though the portions are quite small. Today we got shrimp & grit, TJ breakfast bowl. Highly recommend if you want something new. Not very busy during the morning.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "C M",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Every worker we came in contact with was friendly. Our waitress did a good job. Food was reasonably priced, delicious and came out in a timely manner.  Save room for the salted caramel cheesecake",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Katherine",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The best restaurant we ate at in gulf shores! We found parking really easily however we went around 4pm. Environment was super colorful and the place was decorated with duct tape. Immediately got seated and food came out quickly. Our waitress, Katie, was super nice and we joked around and got to meet “manager in charge of the day” Bryan! Staff was super sweet and nice. I got the steamed crab legs and it was super good as well as the butter, corn, and potatoes!!!!!! The rest of my party loved wha",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "JG",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Nice waterfront breakfast.  I went here on Monday for breakfast. They weren't busy, got seated and drink order taken immediately.  Very friendly staff.  I ordered the Shrimp Omelette.  It was really good, the seasoning on the shrimp was excellent. I also got a Bloody Mary, which was good, but I really enjoyed the pickled green beans that were in it.  If you want to have a nice, relaxed, waterfront breakfast this is the place. Would highly recommend for locals or visitors.",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
