  {
    "place_id": "ChIJXQxIx7cEmogRDAn4DNfCXGw",
    "name": "Papa Rocco's",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "101 W 6th Ave, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-7262",
    "website": "https://paparoccos.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=7808330082844936460",
    "lat": 30.2524618,
    "lng": -87.6894741,
    "plus_code": "7826+X6 Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.2,
    "reviews_count": 3085,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Jamie Powell",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Papa Rocco's is always welcoming place to go. Food is always great no matter what I order. Crab legs, pizzas, lasagna, steak, wings and peel and eat shrimp. Definitely worth a visit!! Lunch specials are cheap also and can't beat the live music. We also love to watch football on the weekends here as there are plenty of TVs and games on.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Gina Carter",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "What an awesome lunch! We sat on their new front patio and celebrated our 7 months of sobriety while enjoying a NA Bush and deluxe pizza! The potato skins were amazing.\n\nLastly, Dan was the BEST server ever. So attentive, the order was perfect and he never let our drinks go empty!",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jeff Greenwell",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "Got this while on vacation. Thought we would give a local spot a chance with all the decent reviews. Pizza was undercooked, almost no sauce or cheese. Very undersized for being a “14 inch” pizza. $55 for 3 pizzas and dominos would have been better. Also not a good experience with the person on the phone taking orders. Take your business elsewhere if you want decent pizza. Not sure of other menu items.",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Lynnette Foulk",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "It was so loud the waitress could not hear our orders. The Dr Pepper tasted funny, never got a new one. The waitress said she knew it would take awhile to fix it and offered a different drink. The food… wow, it was quite the let down. Based on the reviews I was surprised by how bland it was. It took a solid 45 minutes to get our order. My son’s wings came out cold. Between the waitresses not acknowledging ANYONE nor the other staff it took longer to explain that the food was cold. For the 1.5 ho",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Robin Settle",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This was a fun place! It is basically a sports bar that serves great food. I had the manicotti with Alfredo sauce and my husband had the All Meat pizza.  Both were excellent, as was our appetizer, the stuffed mushrooms.  Though they were technically stuffed, they were really more like 'filled' (think gooey pizza topping - really good!).\n\nThe atmosphere was relaxed, the service was wonderful, and they even had live entertainment that night.\n\nAs we were leaving, we saw the sign to 'Feed the Fish' ",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
