  {
    "place_id": "ChIJX-UjrECvkIgRIWzBc4_nZGI",
    "name": "Lillian’s Pizza",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "14514 Perdido Key Dr, Pensacola, FL 32507, USA",
    "phone": "+1 850-492-0131",
    "website": "http://www.lillianspizza.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=7090046316696398881",
    "lat": 30.2960107,
    "lng": -87.44524609999999,
    "plus_code": "7HW3+CW Pensacola, FL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 3309,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Traci Pryhuber",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "OMG! 6 years in the south and we'd all but given up on a pizza that would meet our Chicago standards. Sorry it took so long, Lillians! Not only was the thin crust amd pan pizza on point,  the homemade meatballs were juicy and so flavorful.  Don't get me started on the marinara 🤤\nYou're missing out if you haven't tried this place! We will be back and back and back!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "H. Hays",
        "rating": 2,
        "text": "Had very high expectations for this place after all the fan fair surrounding the place. Well the reality did not live up to the hype. Had planned on bringing a group here next week and thought we would try it out first. Arrived just after opening and was seated promptly. Ordered the house made meatballs as an appetizer. Found them very very spicy and very dense. They also had hard inedible chunks of meat on the outside. My wife ordered the club sandwich which came with mayo on the side. I've nev",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Chris Martin",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Food was alright. Prices were pretty steep for what we ordered. Staff was friendly and quick. I had the meatball sub and this is only my opinion, but the meatballs were way too big for the sandwich. I had to cut it up which would've been fine but the plate I was given was a basket with tissue paper on the bottom. So needless to say, before every bite I had to be sure there was no paper. The pizzas were good. Pepperoni and cheese. Wings were decent. Kids icees were 20 bucks just for a souvenir cu",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Featherbear19",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "We picked up a pizza on our way back from the beach because we heard it was a great place. We ordered it online and it was easy to do, they let us know when it was ready. We love thin crust because we were born and raised in Chicago. So we thought the flavor was great, spices, sauce, amount of toppings was on point however we all thought that the crust was a bit too thin, for our liking. Would we get it again while in the area? Absolutely. Just needed a bit more to hold all of the goodness. Othe",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mitchell Younts",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Came on a Sunday afternoon. Our waitress Andrea was very helpful and attentive. She let us know we would enjoy the meatballs appetizer and was right, then helped us find the right shirt for my son. Pizza was really good, not just average but really good. Drinks were reasonably priced. Overall good experience. We will be back.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      }
    ],
