  {
    "place_id": "ChIJjUVMSMMFmogRb0-XfuWyIEY",
    "name": "Ginny Lane Bar and Grill",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "4851 Wharf Pkwy E suite D100-D106, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-224-6500",
    "website": "http://ginnylanebargrill.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=5053235480650796911",
    "lat": 30.2947865,
    "lng": -87.6292596,
    "plus_code": "79VC+W7 Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.1,
    "reviews_count": 1605,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Marilyn Washburn",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Decided to try a place we hadn't been to before and we're so glad we did! The food was absolutely delicious (pecan crusted chicken, baked oysters in truffle and garlic, calamari, grouper topped with lump crab, and fried crab claws)!!\nI've actually had better claws but they were still good. 👍🏼\nIt was lovely dining outside on Portage Creek and inside offered live music with a cozy, elegant atmosphere.\nOur service was fast and friendly...wonderful off-season experience! 🥰",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Carol Lengerman",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "GREAT HAPPY HOUR MENU from 11-6pm\n\nShrimp special today: $20 all you can eat and comes with Cole slaw, hush puppies, and fries. Oysters were $1/apiece.  They were small but had good flavor.\n\nJustin was a great waiter and we tipped him accordingly, but the bar service was unbelievably slow considering the staff to patron ratio was at least 2:1.\n\nGreat view of the ICW and yachts on the wharf.\n\nThis was not our first time here, and we were surprised at how run down it seemed.  With so many dining o",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Whitney Prince",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had a wonderful experience! My husband and his dad went fishing this morning on the pier and caught a cooler full of Red Drum, but we had no way to clean and cook it. GL has a \"hook and cook\" service so we called ahead and spoke to Clint. He was super helpful and told us to bring them in and they would clean and cook them for us. From the moment we walked in the door, everyone was so friendly and kind. Clint scooped up our cooler and took the fish to the back to clean and prep them himself. W",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Zoe Gehman",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great live music on Friday night! Very extensive menu with great options. Had a frozen watermelon margarita, gumbo (absolutely amazing) and jalapeño focaccia",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brian M",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Food was ok.  Had the Bayou Grouper.  Not bad, but not great for the price.  Nice happy hour though.  We might go back during happy hour, but pick other items.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      }
    ],
