  {
    "place_id": "ChIJT1B1BGkGmogRQCkjQHXktLU",
    "name": "Brick & Spoon - Orange Beach",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "24705 Canal Rd, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-981-7772",
    "website": "https://www.brickandspoon.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=13093341208911227200",
    "lat": 30.290855,
    "lng": -87.6028536,
    "plus_code": "79RW+8V Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.6,
    "reviews_count": 2366,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "H. Hays",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This place was pretty busy for 10:30 on a Wednesday and we found out why! We were seated immediately upon entering.  Drinks brought out within minutes and order taken. Food was expedited with speed and precision. My wife ordered the patty melt, which was so hot she burnt her lip. My tacos were loaded with blackened shrimp and a perfect amount of seasoning. The Fries were hot and more addictive than that fast food place with a big M in its name. Our waitress Carolyn B was fast and efficient all w",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Wanietta Stuckey",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We arrived at Brick & Spoon for breakfast at 9:45 and we're seated immediately. The menu is big with a good variety. They serve cirn or cheese grits with almost all of their breakfast choices. My husband ordered the Traditional Eggs Benedict and breakfast potatoes. He had hoped for it to be on a homemade biscuit but it was on an English muffin. He said it was really good. I ordered the Western Scrambler with fruit. I got the berry fruit rather than the melon fruit. Delish! I couldn't eat all of ",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Eunice Watters",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Absolutely Amazing Experience!\n\nIf you’re in Gulf Shores and looking for a place that delivers on every level, Brick & Spoon is it!\n\nFrom the moment we walked in, the customer service was warm, welcoming, and genuinely friendly. The staff made us feel appreciated and taken care of the entire time. You can tell they truly enjoy what they do.\n\nNow let’s talk about the food… WOW. Everything was perfectly cooked and incredibly well-seasoned. Every bite was flavorful, fresh, and beautifully presented",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Marialexandraa Ochoa",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The food was fantastic. The restaurant was great but what really impressed us was the server. We were on our way out of alabama and got here at opening hour.  About 4 other groups walked in and she absolutely killed it. Nikki needs a raise. We got outstanding service and the food and drinks were a bonus! Make this stop if you're ever in town!",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Bobbi Masino",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The Brick & Spoon was delicious.  My husband and I went in for a late breakfast and really enjoyed our selections. I had the Fried Steak Breakfast which came on top of a delicious biscuit with gravy. Over easy eggs and a delicious spicy honey drizzle. My husband got the Cajun Shrimp Benny which came with a side of potatoes. He really enjoyed the entree the potatoes were just potatoes. The star of the show was the breakfast fries. That came covered in gravy, diced tomatoes, a Sunnyside egg on top",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      }
    ],
