  {
    "place_id": "ChIJCxKZ9JEHmogRuCelDFh3O64",
    "name": "Cactus Cantina Perdido Beach Blvd",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "25311 Perdido Beach Blvd, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-981-4628",
    "website": "http://mycactuscantina.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=12554759606278367160",
    "lat": 30.2688435,
    "lng": -87.59269599999999,
    "plus_code": "7C94+GW Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.2,
    "reviews_count": 2638,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Vikas Chilkuri",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Nice place, we went at 4 something relatively slow.. but in an hour it filled up and it was busy by 5!!\nThe food was great, lots of familiar dishes, but they also have a few unique ones, not found in your usual local hometown mexican joint.\nLeroy our server was great, not too overbearing and just the right amount of checking in! Overall I'll recommend to anyone and will probably go back when we are in the area again.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Dil Singh",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Food was okay, not many vegan options. Drinks where amazing! Didn't like they changed extra cause we wanted spicy salsa. The chips and salsa were kind of bland. I order the shrimp tacos and definitely needed some of the hot sauce. Wife got vegan tacos and didn't like it as much",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Gloria Holmes-Palmer",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This restaurant is wonderful.   Our waitress Ashton was so helpful in deciding which meal best fit our taste.  She was right.  I had the grilled shrimp tacos and my husband had the pineapple fajitas. The next time we go back to Ocean Beach, we will go back to this restaurant.   Ashton you are the best!",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "R Farmland",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Excellent food. But the chips were a little weird. They were very thin and tasteless. And the salsa was ketchupy. But the chicken was excellent and reasonably priced.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Sheley White",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The food is amazing 🤩 and the price was cheap. The bathroom could have felt a little cleaner but the place is busy. The decorations were great and a lot of little kids were there with the families and they seemed to really like it so I would say it's a good family atmosphere. The bar was nice and had plenty of drinks to choose from. The salsa is spicy I loved it. I even paid 53¢ for extra spicy sauce. I had taken it out, so I carried it back to the room. I had the deluxe nachos with shredded chi",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
