  {
    "place_id": "ChIJi-22Ig6okIgR28UIl3DUZLg",
    "name": "OSO at Bear Point Harbor - Orange Beach",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "5749 Bay La Launch Ave, Orange Beach, AL 36561, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-345-6738",
    "website": "https://osobearpoint.com/?utm_source=google",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=13286978380685166043",
    "lat": 30.309428,
    "lng": -87.5260498,
    "plus_code": "8F5F+QH Orange Beach, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 1577,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Daneen England",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Definitely one of the better restaurants that we’ve been to. We had grilled snapper as well as blackened grouper and black and shrimp. Also the bang bang shrimp. The Asian slow coleslaw was fantastic. Hush puppies were spot on. The service was top-notch. The restaurant is super cute. Lots of little chickens running around outside. The kid really loved being able to put the bear and sit out outside with the bear in the skeleton. It’s on the water the boats. The food was excellent and I will defin",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Karen Simmons",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "I recently took a girls trip to Orange Beach and we tried OSO at Bear Point. We sat outside and the view was amazing. We watched as boats came in and had a beautiful sunset. We shared fried pickles as an app, which were good. I had the bang bang shrimp bowl which was amazing. Everyone in my party raved about their entrees. We will definitely be back. The live music was great, as well. Highly recommend.",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "William Wright",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Came down to Oso on Bear Point today. Cool-laid back local vibe. Island time for sure. With great service. Has Happy Hour Monday-Friday from 2-6pm. $1.50 Busch Lights and cocktails. Bartenders are very friendly and attentive. They also have live music every night after 6pm. Outside. Inside-outside seating, patio seating outside inside, upstairs seating. This place is huge! Probably the coolest menu I’ve seen on the island yet! Menu is decently priced with awesome specials. Chef Ashton came out a",
        "time": "10 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "John Jones",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This was an absolutely wonderful dining experience!\nWe had a server, Ricardo, who had one of the friendliest and kindest smiles in all of south Alabama. His service was top tier and should be the standard of measure.\nThe food was phenomenal. It came out hot and fresh and very quick to the table from the time of order.\nWe had the blackened chicken tots, and the shrimp and crawfish nachos, and the grouper nuggets. The food was the best we've had all week! The grouper was fresh and delicious. I hig",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Connie Churchill",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Loved this place. Great food, you can tell that the chef loves his/her job. The food really tastes good and looks good. We listened to a band afterward at the bar area, and it was a good time! Will always go back when I'm visiting Gulf Shores/Orange Beach!",
        "time": "12 months ago"
      }
    ],
