  {
    "place_id": "ChIJneMmQjkFmogRaOGq8IDwudg",
    "name": "Gulf Shores Diner",
    "type": "restaurant",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "3639 Gulf Shores Pkwy #4, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-0088",
    "website": "",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?cid=15616777619468116328",
    "lat": 30.2955989,
    "lng": -87.6837997,
    "plus_code": "78W8+6F Gulf Shores, AL, USA",
    "rating": 4.6,
    "reviews_count": 1775,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Rosefaith Masterpiece",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The food was absolutely amazing. I went with the Philly Steak Omelet, and it did not disappoint. It was packed with flavor, perfectly cooked, and the portion size was filling.\nArwa made the experience standout. Her service was excellent. She was genuine, welcoming, and the kind of hospitality that makes you feel like a regular even on your first visit. Everyone is so kind and welcoming.\nI would definitely come back.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mary Steinacker-Grimm",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This place is like coming home to family. In the year and a half that I have been eating at the Gulf Shores Diner on Sunday mornings with my parents, I literally feel like we are coming to the best place to have a meal on Sundays. All the staff treat us like family. The food is always delicious. The restaurant is always clean. You can buy local art. The menu is diverse and always made fresh.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rob Huey",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "No frills diner with good food, service and lots of options.\n\nMy brother-in-law (lives in this area) recommended this to me and I tried it this morning for breakfast. Andrew waited on me and he did an excellent job of making sure I had everything I needed. The food came out quickly and everything tasted great. It was a very good experience.\n\nThey also feature art from local artists which is very cool. I would definitely recommend stopping by here for breakfast.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Cruzana Hall",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "If I could give this place a negative rating I would. It started off by waiting for almost 30 mins for someone to take our order. They did apologize. We finally ordered the food and let me say it was the worst food ever. Order a hamburger and to be honest I don’t think that was even a burger patty. It had no flavor had a nasty taste to it. also ordered the Philly cheese steak and that was over cooked way too salty. The chicken sandwich the tomato was thicker than the chicken itself. The fries ha",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "JG",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Nice Relaxing Breakfast. Went here for breakfast on a Tuesday.  The service was immediate and pleasant.  I ordered the Philly Steak Omelette.  It was very flavorful and cooked perfect.  The hash browns were good too. If you want a local, relaxed place to have a great breakfast. This is the place.",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
