  {
    "place_id": "ChIJh2iBU6RBmogR5qiJV0bndWY",
    "name": "Rock Creek Golf Club",
    "type": "activity_accommodation",
    "city": "Gulf Shores",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "140 Clubhouse Dr, Fairhope, AL 36532, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-928-4223",
    "website": "https://bit.ly/3rvTSn2",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.5739196,-87.8869132",
    "lat": 30.5739196,
    "lng": -87.8869132,
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 368,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "owen Utsey",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Rock Creek Golf Club in Fairhope, Alabama is one of the most enjoyable and well-maintained golf courses on the Eastern Shore. The course layout is both challenging and fun, making it a great option for golfers of all skill levels. Each hole offers a unique design with tree-lined fairways, well-place",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Ben Moseley",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "I wanted to share some honest feedback regarding my recent experience at your facility. Unfortunately, my visit was disappointing on multiple levels.\nFirst, the condition of the greens was very poor — far below what one would expect from a course charging $100 per round. Based on the quality of play",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Roger Patteson",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "I love this course. Carts are fast. Beverage cart personnel is flattering. Many holes with a lot of elevation challenges. Fairways and greens are a nice 9/10. The tee boxes could use some work but it’s just that time of the year where we’re all out there regularly tearing them up. The venue itself i",
        "time": "4 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "j fish",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Loved this course. Lots of elevation changes, greens are quick but true. Course facilities are very nice, staff was friendly, engaging and helpful. We played there while on vacation. If I lived there, I would become a member. We got a chance to talk with some of the regulars there, and they were fri",
        "time": "3 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Celia Nuñez",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Gorgeous place to live at, specially if you love golf, quietness, nature, and you can afford over 800k dollar home :)",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      }
    ],
