  {
    "place_id": "ChIJocYu8wYFmogRWwAiSn2fhRg",
    "name": "The Sloop",
    "type": "activity_accommodation",
    "city": "Gulf Shores",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "103 W Canal Dr, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-500-1007",
    "website": "https://www.thesloop.biz/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.277591,-87.6872061",
    "lat": 30.277591,
    "lng": -87.6872061,
    "rating": 4.7,
    "reviews_count": 1490,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Kyle Filiatreault",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Why has this place not been on my radar sooner? This a a great spot where it seems as if locals are the consistent patron.  The cheese steak is now my new #1.  I prefer cheese whiz, but you can pick provolone if you’d like.  The fish dip was the weekly special and I it was delicious. I’ll be perusin",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Tim Katanski",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great bar, makes you feel like you belong.  Sports bar, great spot to watch the big game. The cheesesteak w/ cheese whiz was fantastic! Cheesesteak egg rolls were a great warm up. The homemade chips that come with the sandwich are perfect. Topped the meal off with a Painkiller and the Sloop made din",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Pond Hockey Queen",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Cold beer, surprisingly solid Philly cheesesteak, and total hole-in-the-wall vibes,  in the best way!!!  Eclectic, laid-back, and exactly what you want after a beach day. Definitely coming back next time there’s live music 🎶🍻",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kebrina Harrison",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "My family and I visited on Fall Break and we loved this little hole in the wall. We were looking for something a little different than the tourist traps off the beach and this place did not disappoint. The waitress was sweet and did a great job. She was very impressive as she did not even have to wr",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "The Chef’s View",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nIf you are anywhere near Gulf Shores and you love a good Philly cheesesteak, you absolutely have to stop by The Sloop. I cannot say enough about how good this sandwich was. I went with the cheese whiz because that’s how the real ones in Philly are traditionally made and I am so glad I did. Th",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      }
    ],
