  {
    "place_id": "ChIJ7XYsPq4FmogRAQe7ss69R_I",
    "name": "Woodside Restaurant",
    "type": "activity_accommodation",
    "city": "Gulf Shores",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "20249 State Park Rd, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-923-3100",
    "website": "http://woodsideatgsp.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.2667117,-87.6795341",
    "lat": 30.2667117,
    "lng": -87.6795341,
    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 1095,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Krystal Burnett",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Excellent! We were wowed by the delicious quality food and dining experience here. From the big portions of smoked ribs and perfect potato salad, to the house made sausages and smoky pimento cheese, and then the wow factor crusted goat cheese salad with candied jalapeños, berries, and house made fig",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "The Chef’s View",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️\n\nOur visit to Gulf State Park in Gulf Shores, Alabama was an unforgettable day from start to finish. We started the morning by renting e-bikes from a local company called Paradise Pedal LLC, and it could not have gone more smoothly. The owner was one of the kindest and most accommodating ",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brian M",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great place right in the state park.  We went from our campsite by bike.  You never leave the trail going there.  Great happy hour, food, and live music on the weekends.  We went twice during out time there.  We will be going again for sure on our next trip to Gulf Shores.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "A R",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Overall, it's a great spot to grab a bite after a hike or bike ride. I ordered a Caesar salad, which tasted good, but was surprised to be charged $8 for a small piece of chicken—making the total around $20. That felt a bit steep. Also, it's unclear whether you're supposed to grab your own utensils a",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mary S",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Delicious food and beautiful park!  Smokehouse Club Sammie and fresh Kettle chips with Christmas tunes playing low. Check out Eagles Nest Cabins when you're over this way. Touring the park trails via ebike is crazy fun!",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      }
    ],
