    "reviews_count": 772,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Janice Robbins",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This is a great place on Hwy 98 in Lillian, Alabama. Food was really good. Entertainment made it fun to be there. We met the owner and his wife and great people and I even got to meet the Marlboro poster guy! How cool! Worth the drive to have a little fun and enjoy some good food! Cool atmosphere! I",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Dave Hazlett",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Little bar/restaurant hole in the wall but you won't be disappointed. Great food/atmosphere craw fish boil every sat with live music and Tony the bartender was awesome. Wish we would have found it sooner",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Christy Oyer",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Let's go! While this restaurant is a hole in the wall, dive and needs some updating. The staff here is amazing. While I cannot give the \"owner\" as much props, if it wasn't for the music, workers and the locals, we would never go back. To my favorite chef, Robert: if you love Grouper, get the Grouper",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Sadly Ignored",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Really just the best place EVER!  Great food... get the blackened grouper!  Great Music! Midlife crisis or sum such shit! Price is right. Service is great!!! Always a pleasure!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Tom Ignas",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Stopped by for a quick lunch while running a job nearby. Great service, great food & great atmosphere. What else can you say?!?  We need more places like this. The firecracker shrimp is the bomb and the oysters are not too shabby.",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      }
    ],
