    "lng": -87.6877932,
    "rating": 4.3,
    "reviews_count": 389,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Rebecca Murphy",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Shrimpy’s was an okay experience. The mini golf was on par with most smaller golf places around the area. But don’t be fooled by “it’s the cheapest”. We had 6 people and brought the “buy 1 get 1 half-off” coupon, thinking we would pay full price for 3 and half price for 3 - thus, the most affordable",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rachel Sauder",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "We've gone to eat there twice in the last month.  The first time we waited over an hour for our food (they mixed up the order), this last time it was around 35 minutes for 2 sandwiches and fries, so not a place to grab a quick bite. Both times the lady working explained she was understaffed.  Seems ",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Madan Nagaraju",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Very well maintained mini-18 hole golf course. It's fun, attractive and just enough time to go through the course.\n\nThe ice cream shop and the dining area is well kept, there are clean restrooms inside.\nThey charge $10 for adult and $7 for kids, you could pickup the clubs and the golf ball inside al",
        "time": "4 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Sarah MeLinne Mancinelli",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Shrimpy's Mini Golf Course has been updated since I last went years ago. It's a really nice course now and very family friendly. My 6 year old was able to play with my husband and I and our 2 year old tried! Overall fun for the family and not overly crowded or expensive.",
        "time": "2 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Sarah Livengood",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Mini golf was not all that involved, but a fun way to spend half an hour. It was $10 per adult for mini gulf. The food was decently priced, great portion sizes, but minimal flavor. I ordered the chicken bacon ranch fries and they tasted like nothing other than ranch, even with fried chicken on it, t",
        "time": "2 years ago"
      }
    ],
