    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 3349,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Rafe Bar",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The food was great! Ambiance and service were great as well. We got a dozen chargrilled oysters as an appetizer, along with the crab cake, hush puppies, and fried crab legs,all delicious, especially the oysters. There’s a sauce that came with the appetizers and it was really good, I used that as a d",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "William Wright",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The BEST Chargrilled Oysters IVE HAD EAST OF NEW ORLEANS! Not fishy at all if you want to try oysters for the first time. Right on the canal! I also had to try the Pontchartrain which was amazing and Mark recommended as well as the boo fries which I’ll try next time. The beer is cold and the views a",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kimberley Cannon-Franklin",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Marvelous Louisiana style, flare and decor as well Flavor, seasoning and preparation of foods. Everything was super fresh, seafood included.\nBeautiful outside dining available with sandy and lawn area overlooking the river.",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Bridget Schott",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Angela was an amazing server. She was attentive without being overbearing, and got us just what we needed, almost immediately. Food was stupid good ! Im obsessed and will be telling everyone",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Phil Hoose",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The food and drinks were wonderful and our server Amy was fantastic. She led us through the menu and made great suggestions. Acme Oyster House is worth it.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      }
    ],
