    "rating": 4.1,
    "reviews_count": 213,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Daniel Latham",
        "rating": 2,
        "text": "If you've been out all day or drunk as hell and are really really hungry it's edible. Nachos got that weird cheap frozen \"grilled\" chicken, canned jalapenos, and fake cheese. Ballpark style. Pizza about as good as chuck e cheese pizza or something similar. Street corn was good tho, tore that up",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Morgan Biggins",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Ron was absolutely amazing! He is the reason why we will be headed back there tomorrow. He recommended the fish and it was amazing.",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jessica Partain",
        "rating": 2,
        "text": "First and only time. Pizza was okay, burger was a premade frozen patty (not so much as salt on it) and the bywater nacho’s were mediocre at best (from the canned cheese, three different kinds of unseasoned meat and not so great chips). 4.6 out of 5 star reviews, how? Maybe we just ordered three wron",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Justin Cotten",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Stopped in for drinks and the scenery. Nice place, the view was nice overlooking the ocean.  It's a good walk be prepared when going here. You have to pay to walk the pier. Neat place to stop in and have a drink. If it's cool out make sure to have a long sleeve shirt, especially if the wind's blowin",
        "time": "3 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Shannon (NOLA Gent)",
        "rating": 2,
        "text": "This is the restaurant located at the Gulf State Park Fishing Pier. The seating is all open air with a roof overhead along with a nice view of the beach and Gulf. The best thing about this place would be the view. The food left a lot to be desired and they served me a VERY mediocre burger then to ad",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      }
    ],
