  {
    "place_id": "ChIJXzPo0MYFmogRapZQ9PNOme0",
    "name": "The Galway Irish Public House",
    "category": "specialty",
    "city": "Gulf Shores",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "2301 E 2nd St, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-339-2150",
    "website": "http://www.galwayirishpub.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.2757298,-87.6834549",
    "lat": 30.2757298,
    "lng": -87.6834549,
    "rating": 4.7,
    "reviews_count": 477,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Rob Smith",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Sat outside and had a very attentive server. The food we ordered was above our expectations. Everything was phenomenal and would eat it again. The only thing I would say, was the cole slaw dressing in the chicken sandwich made it very messy to eat. In my opinion, I would recommend that on the side. ",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "G Man",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "The experience at Galway was pretty good.   Food was ok.  Nothing spectacular, and perhaps just a little above average.   The fish and chips were okay.  The fish did come out hot, and it was fresh tasting but it was also a tad bland.   I'm not a big fan of salt, but it definitely needed more.   The ",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Thomas Martin",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Genuine Irish pub atmosphere.\nGreat selection of beers and spirits with terrific service. The Reuben is decent; the home fries are PERFECT! Don't sleep on those fries🤤",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "J McGaha",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Great find in Gulf shores, not the typical tourist trap. Not the cheapest place in the area a little on the pricier side, but a great value for the quality of food and service received. Service was excellent, not overbearing, inattentive, or rude. Frozen Irish coffees were perfect. The pretzel with ",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "hss1121",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "My husband and I absolutely loved everything about our visit to The Galway! The food was out of this world! We loved everything we ordered but the St. Patty melt was our favorite by far. So much flavor and a great portion size. Also, the atmosphere and service were spot on.",
        "time": "a year ago"
      }
    ],
