  {
    "place_id": "ChIJldilw7YEmogRn4r2cQ38KF8",
    "name": "The Steamer Baked Oyster Bar",
    "category": "specialty",
    "city": "Gulf Shores",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "124 W 1st Ave, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-4042",
    "website": "https://gulfcoaststeamer.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.2495445,-87.6905347",
    "lat": 30.2495445,
    "lng": -87.6905347,
    "rating": 3.9,
    "reviews_count": 2525,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Ashley Morikawa",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Good place for large groups to sit inside or outside on the patio and have many options for seafood and also non-seafood options. We got a table pretty quickly for a group of 8. I really wanted baked oysters and they have an option to mix baked oyster flavors. I tried the cajun, mexican and parmesan",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Saydie Hughes",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The oysters were YUM! We ordered only oysters and drinks! And my 2 yr old enjoyed his strawberry and banana slushi! Definitely will come back next time we are down for more",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Will E.",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "The Steamers Baked Oyster Bar offered a good dining experience. Their shrimp was particularly enjoyable, and the food quality overall was good, complemented by good service. While the Gulf location suggested better seafood pricing, we found the prices relatively high. The atmosphere was slightly und",
        "time": "10 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mark Pillow",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Found Steamers almost by accident and so glad we did. Tucked just behind the giant souvenir store on the main intersection in Gulf Shores, It was a Monday night and we sat on the patio (covered and screened) and were seated right away. Very comfortable and casual. The food was all very good. We had ",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Dawn B",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Yes I know, I know…. You don’t go to the beach for crab legs but I did and they were great! We love eating here each time we come to OBA/Gulf Shores.",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      }
    ],
