    "reviews_count": 31,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Matt",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "I ate here and loved it! Gulf Shores was in need of restaurant with this level of food excellence. The restaurant is located in the new Embassy Suites hotel. It is well-designed and elegant while maintaining the coastal atmosphere. You have a beautiful view of the Gulf from the restaurant.\n\nI had th",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brandon Styles Live",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Manita was a wonderful server, she was very friendly, professional and attentive. We got the pork chop, grouper, kids grilled cheese, a virgin daiquiri and key lime pie. We'll definitely be back. The view is amazing too!",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Dr. Do Little",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "Atmosphere was great. You can see the beach and the sunset. The food was bad. No flavor and the chicken we ordered was pink. The watermelon salad had badly any salad. For the price they charged...looks like someone was stealing.",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Selina Thome",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Lovely dinner with friends. The blackened grouper with coconut rice and edamame succotash was fresh and delicious! Our friend said the pork chop was too.We had cocktails and wine also.\nI have celiac disease. I called before we arrived and the chef called me back to discuss my options. She was so kno",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Amanda Blackwell",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had a wonderful experience at Tide & Table and will definitely be back. Great service, atmosphere, and food. Went with a group and got the crab cake, ceviche, and fried green tomato appetizers— all were delicious. I got the shrimp and sausage pasta for my entree, and it was amazing. We tried alll",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      }
