    "category": "specialty",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "601 W Beach Blvd, Gulf Shores, AL 36542, USA",
    "phone": "+1 251-948-2100",
    "website": "http://www.bahamabobs.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.2463987,-87.6986501",
    "lat": 30.2463987,
    "lng": -87.6986501,
    "rating": 4.5,
    "reviews_count": 4365,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Andrea Van Someren",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We definitely arrived during shift change, still didn’t wait for a table/server. Our server was very kind and made a mistake ringing up my order… no biggy for me, however, I’m pretty sure she told the cook to give me more shrimp for the mistake or something… if not, then they give you A TON of shrim",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Ciji Sabo",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We can here on a Sunday night in December, and the place was packed-a good sign from the start. Even with the crowd, service was quick, and our server was very friendly. The portions were fairly large, and the food was great. But please remember, YOU MUST SAVE ROOM FOR DESSERT! We tried the key lime",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "kaylie berrong",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Had the pecan crusted flounder and the gumbo and everything was delicious! It came out fast and was hot and fresh. Dylan was our server and he was great. Margaritas were 10/10, light and not too sweet.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Sheila Wyatt",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Very loud inside seating. We enjoyed the patio with heaters. Hostess was friendly, waitress was friendly. Gumbo was delicious but the steamed shrimp lacked flavor.",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "C J",
