    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Frank Lapcheske",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Amazing place and great food,  it is awesome. I come here weekly and love the people, the management and staff. Absolutely the best Ruebin ever and Patricia was an amazing bartender. You are missing out if you don’t try this place. The schnitzel is amazing",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Leigh E",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We are snowbirding in Foley and decided to give this place a shot.  The chicken schnitzel is delicious as well as the pretzel and we are not big eaters, sharing an entree.  The chef splits our meals up on different plates (without asking) .  It's our go to place to go to now.  Great happy our specia",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mary Henry",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Wow what a great local find!  I can't say enough good things about this spot. From the moment we walked in, we were treated like regulars —even though it was our first visit. Patrise was incredibly knowledgeable about the beers on tap and the food they had available and was happy to offer recommenda",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rick Chesser",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The BEST german based eatery i’ve had!!! Braut’s & kraut were delicious, pretzel appetizer was so tender and the schnitzel was truly Devine!! Comfortable environment, the staff was nothing less than fantastic. A perfect lunch time dining experience",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Joe H",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The Bier Shack is under new ownership, and they are absolutely knocking it out of the park! It’s so much more than just axe throwing now—it’s a full-on destination. They’ve managed to create a fun, friendly environment that feels welcoming the moment you walk in.\n​The addition of German food and a g",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      }
