    "reviews_count": 88,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Brew Dude",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This was our 2nd experience there. Every bit as good as the first. The charcuterie board is one of the best we've had anywhere! ALSO one of the few (if-not-only)area  establishments that has the class to offer Edmund's Oast beers - NICE!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kevin Rosborough",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We happened to find this little gem hiding at OWA; be sure and talk to Holly the owner and sommelier; she knows her wine; the selection is superb; have a charcuterie plate and enjoy a wonderful experience tasting some great international wines",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "tommy 454",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐\n\nWho knew a late-night food quest could lead to such a hidden gem? We stumbled into C'est Le Vin in Foley, Alabama, because, well, it was late and options were scarce. But boy, are those 5-star reviews right!\n\nWe came strictly for the food, and let me tell you, it did not disappoint. The dishe",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Claudia Lewis",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This was absolutely the cutest wine bar ever! You can make your own Charcuterie board and enjoy great drinks. Went for a date night and it was just perfect. The prices were very reasonable and they had some really great choices for the boards. This was a neat experience and very worth trying! The se",
        "time": "2 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Elise Hatten",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Eddie and Austin were awesome! The charcuterie boards were great (especially the goat cheese). My husband had the smoked Blade and Bow old fashioned, and I had the Forbidden Sour and Italian Margarita. Drinks were great!! We will be back.",
        "time": "3 years ago"
      }
    ],
