    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Jrock",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Nice little jaunt led us to this gem of a brewery.  Atmosphere was laid back with pleasant decor.  Fun tin tackers abound and they even have aplenty for purchase. Like most craft breweries there are hits and misses across the menu based upon personal preferences of the particular patron.  The flagsh",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Malcolm Earhart",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "A nice brewery in suburban Alabama, I stopped on my way to Orange Beach.  I arrived early on a Friday so it wasn't busy.  I grabbed a seat at the bar and had several half pours while I read a little.  I stuck to my usual pattern of ales and ipas.  The fairhope was fairly dry, a nice departure from a",
        "time": "11 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Joseph Raczynski",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Good range of beers - all about average with respect to their specific categories. The service was a little weird - meaning not as aware of people looking for service, even though they weren't too busy. It was probably just the night.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jay",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Great selection of beers—whether you’re into lagers, porters, sours, or seltzers, there’s something for everyone. Normally this would be an easy 5-star spot for me, but the bartender today really missed the mark. Zero personality, borderline rude. I left while she was mid-convo with a couple she cle",
        "time": "10 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mikey Kay (Fire & Smoke BBQ Company)",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We had a great time at fairhope brewing company. We went on a Saturday night and they had live music and great beer can you really ask for more. The staff was super nice and answered all the beer questions you could have. The atmosphere was great just a ton of people have fun and drinking great beer",
        "time": "3 years ago"
      }
