    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Dana",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Came here for the first time today for a wreath making class and it was so much fun fun! The Glühwein was delicious (tastes just like what I used to enjoy in Germany) and my wreath turned out fabulous. Seems like a very friendly place with regulars that have been going there for years. Oh and happy ",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mary Steinacker-Grimm",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Bingo night is fun, it is dog friendly, but there’s a lot of places to explore and sit as well. The staff is super friendly and there’s a board where you can buy a beer for someone who really needs it, like a hospice nurse!",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Ryan Beverly",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This place is pretty awesome, great setting and venue, plenty of outdoor seating on a beautiful day to enjoy the fresh air.  Overall the ambience is very free flowing, nice selection of on tap beers, ( Smoked Gary) is Highly recommended. Also a plethora of other options including wine slushies and s",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jeffrey Cowgill",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Just wow! I’ve been by here many times and finally decided to stop in and check it out.  Totally surprised and happy to see this super cool place out here just off Barrancas. It’s a neat combination of outdoor spaces complete with gardens, a bamboo maze and plenty of shady areas with tables.\n\nUrbanC",
        "time": "9 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mike Hall",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Friendly staff, great beer, great music, and awesome ambience. The food truck was amazing as well! Very easy to get to from the beach, just a short drive.\nThe fire pit was great as it was a chilly night.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      }
