    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Kym Cherry",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "This was some of the best food we had while we were visiting. It was really top notch. If you are at ALL interested in fresh, local seafood I would Highly recommend giving it a try. Unless you are on a strict budget then be Very mindful..\n\nMy daughter stated quite clearly she was looking to spend ar",
        "time": "7 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Aaron Lee",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great seafood market if you don’t want to pay the tourist trap price and tips.  We had shrimps, gumbo, crab cakes, and other sides.  Very good.  Probably saved ~30% compared to a restaurant.",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Peggy Sue M",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Awesome seafood and fantastic service. This is a great find for fresh shrimp or fish in Orange Beach. They are super friendly and helpful. They steam your shrimp for you and have sides of potatoes and corn, add some sausage and bring it back to your place to enjoy. Delicious and inexpensive way to h",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mckenna Patterson",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "This place is our new go-to! Best meal of the trip and most affordable! 10/10 recommend if you like seafood boil. We got the reds and they were so tender. The sausage was also some of the best sausage i’ve ever had in my life.",
        "time": "a year ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Bryce Massey",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "If you want crab legs to eat wherever you are storing this is the place. We have tried them all, and this is our go to from now on. Crab legs were delicious and easy to work with, hush puppies were great, corn was great, shrimp were great, and the surprise of the order were the potatoes. We assumed ",
        "time": "a year ago"
      }
