    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Cam Paulding",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Strawberry butter! I've never heard of it, or had it for the matter, until we ate at Mile Marker 158, and it is interestingly good.\n\nWe showed up on a late Sunday and it was Bingo night. The place was full and I was sure there was going to be a wait. And I was wrong. The hostess immediately greeted ",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "EJ W",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We enjoyed our visit and meal at Mile Marker 158. Set back, near the hotel and marina, it's a nice little place with decent food. The service was quick and they were friendly. It was a weekday though, so not too busy. We had blackened grouper (a little too much spice, but good), and flounder with po",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Amy White",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Mile Marker 158 is a hidden gem! The food is amazing. The bread that was brought out before our meal was wonderful. It was nice and warm and the strawberry butter, oh my! My husband and I enjoyed the fish of the day,  grouper, with gouda smashed potatoes,  green beans topped with lemon beurre blanc.",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Brian M",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Nice view of the water.  Hidden gem in our book.  We went during happy hour.  Dozen oysters for $12.  Drafts $4.  Shrimp scampi $12.   All the food was great.  It's not just the price, it is the food as well.  Very tasty.  At least the scampi.  Either you love oysters or you hate them.  I happen to ",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Rosa Golden",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "My husband and I recently dined at Mile Marker 158 and had a mixed experience. The weather was great but a little windy, and the view of the marina was beautiful. The staff was friendly and attentive.\n\nI ordered the fried grouper, which looked perfect with a golden brown crust, but it was a bit too ",
        "time": "6 months ago"
      }
