    "reviews_count": 743,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "j mcmanus",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Stopped in at Salty Pearl while out driving around and it ended up being one of the best lunch decisions I’ve made in a long time. The shrimp were hands-down some of the best I’ve ever had—perfectly seasoned, cooked just right, and full of flavor. The hush puppies were incredible, and the curly twis",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Fotogirl Travels",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The Bombdiggidy is an understatement! Simply could not get enough of this little restaurant. The Best Ever Seafood around. My boyfriend & I ate here, 5 days out of 6. Shannon took awesome care of us. Do yourself a favor, eat here!\nWe had the oysters; raw & roasted, snow crab clusters, Ruby Red shrim",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jeffrey Cowgill",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Great place I will definitely be visiting again. Sat at the bar up front and had wine, snack and a good chat with Greg one of the owners/managers. They source a good bit of their seafood from Perdido Bay Seafood. Always fresh and delicious!  Service was prompt and very knowledgeable.\n\nThe char-grill",
        "time": "4 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Daniella Lazo",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "The shrimp platter was great! Their fries are so good and crisp. We came on a not-so-busy night, but I can imagine during their busy season it gets crowded. Will come back again!",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Featherbear19",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We were given a recommendation to go here by locals for amazingly fresh seafood and oysters. My goodness are we so glad that we went! We were not very hungry but we plowed through boom boom shrimp, Sampler Oyster platter- charbroiled, Blackened jumbo shrimp, Fried Grouper bites, (the French fries ar",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
