    "rating": 4.4,
    "reviews_count": 5434,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Jeffery Allen",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Received a Facebook ad our first night in gulf shores advertising $.79 raw oysters on tuesdays, which immedietly caught my interest. When we arrived, I received ANOTHER targeted ad for a free appetizer if you sign up for the app. The oysters were perfect, nicely sized and fresh. Their hotsauce was e",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Kelso Quan",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We got into town late and checked into the hotel across the street. Shrimp Basket was one of the few places still open but it was approaching their closing time. We ran over there to see if their kitchen was still open by chance to order some take out. The servers were kind and checked with the kitc",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Uchizi Phakati",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Stopped for lunch while staying at the hotel across the street, and it did not disappoint! The Boom Boom Shrimp was the highlight, crispy, flavorful, and just the right amount of kick. The rest of the food was fresh and delicious too.\n\nService was ok, overly fast but friendly and attentive enough. T",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Wright Cox",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Great meal at the Shrimp Basket, casual welcoming atmosphere. Tyler was very professional and attentive to us and had good recommendations.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Steven Donahoo",
        "rating": 3,
        "text": "Seasoning was great.  We got a two person Boil bag and the shrimp were completely over cooked.  It wasn't cleaned. We were highly disappointed for a $120 meal. Okra was good and a few off the sides,  but I would check every shrimp you have, check and clean it. We ordered our food online, we did not ",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      }
    ],
