  {
    "place_id": "ChIJ5wPbeXW_kIgRU5jLG3QPw7Y",
    "name": "The Grid Arcade Bar",
    "category": "specialty",
    "city": "Orange Beach",
    "state": "AL",
    "address": "2414 N Pace Blvd, Pensacola, FL 32505, USA",
    "phone": "+1 850-563-7800",
    "website": "http://www.thegridarcadepensacola.com/",
    "google_maps_url": "https://maps.google.com/?q=30.4380979,-87.23962980000002",
    "lat": 30.4380979,
    "lng": -87.23962980000002,
    "rating": 4.8,
    "reviews_count": 298,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author": "Alice Caldwell",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "We took a handful of 12 year old boys down to the grid to play arcade games this evening.  All of the kids loved the vintage games and I loved that they played for 3 hours and I only spent $100!\n\nI’m fairly certain that each of the boys smuggled a “titty token” and I’m sure it will be the topic of c",
        "time": "5 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Susie Reviews",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Was my favorite spot when they opened and is still my favorite place to play pinball in Pensacola today.\n\nThe machines are clean, play well and they have a variety. The cabinet games, pool table and air hockey are fun as well.\n\nThe new Full Tilt beer aimed at pinball aficionados is a tasty IPA.\n\nCas",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Chloe Hicks",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Ive always had such a great time at The Grid Arcade Bar in Pensacola over the years!!!! This place blends a nostalgic arcade experience with a unique bar atmosphere. From retro classics like skeeball, air hockey, and pinball — there’s something here for everyone — whether you’re reliving your childh",
        "time": "3 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "nicole rose",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Great retro arcade.  Machines take tokens but many accepted quarters as well. Games were anywhere from 25 cents to a dollar.  Games ranged from old school pinball machines to the classics.  There is also a pool table and air hockey.  You can choose songs to play for a quarter as well.  There was a b",
        "time": "8 months ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Aulman Watford",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "Fantastic spot. Great games, good vibe, exceptional karaoke, and food trucks. Excellent way to spend an evening.\n\nThe people are nice, with a good mix of people on the west side (the best side) and a really fun and inclusive atmosphere.\n\nBring your kids before 8 or 9?  You will all have a ball.",
        "time": "2 months ago"
      }
    ],
